(2935601, 411671, 5354, '<td valign="top">Very cluttered image. Its obvious what the idea is, but the execution let it down. <br/> <br/>Thanks for your PM. I thought I''d come back and clarify a little:<br/>When presenting an image to the viewer/voter there are a few basic principles which help the viewer ''see'' the image. The camera records everything, but the photographer actually uses selective sight during preperation and setup. This selective sight filters out all extraneous detail, all familiar items, everything which is familiar. The viewer on the otherhand is fresh to the scene and the brain like the camera registers every detail on first sight.<br/> <br/>So the photographer has to compensate. It is not sufficient to record the actual, he has to conciously apply the ''junk'' filter and remove distraction. This enables the viewer to ''see'' the intended scene.<br/> <br/>This image suffers from ''overload''. It may be faithful, and exactly what you encounter every morning, but its in ''record'' mode not ''see'' mode.<br/> <br/>Make the life of the viewer simlpe and you will start to achieve what you intend. In your PM you say you want to learn, I hope that helps.</td>', 'Very cluttered image. Its obvious what the idea is, but the execution let it down.  Thanks for your PM. I thought I''d come back and clarify a little:When presenting an image to the viewer/voter there are a few basic principles which help the viewer ''see'' the image. The camera records everything, but the photographer actually uses selective sight during preperation and setup. This selective sight filters out all extraneous detail, all familiar items, everything which is familiar. The viewer on the otherhand is fresh to the scene and the brain like the camera registers every detail on first sight. So the photographer has to compensate. It is not sufficient to record the actual, he has to conciously apply the ''junk'' filter and remove distraction. This enables the viewer to ''see'' the intended scene. This image suffers from ''overload''. It may be faithful, and exactly what you encounter every morning, but its in ''record'' mode not ''see'' mode. Make the life of the viewer simlpe and you will start to achieve what you intend. In your PM you say you want to learn, I hope that helps.', '2006-10-17 02:16:46.000000', NULL, 1),
