(2943605, 410716, 31403, '<td valign="top">the funny little man drew my eye first - pretty big distraction to the story you''re telling here.<br/> <br/>Might also suggest moving the stuff on the bath tub or changing angle so it''s not in the photo.<br/> <br/>Love the creative here - it''s really nice work.  Cute model.</td>', 'the funny little man drew my eye first - pretty big distraction to the story you''re telling here. Might also suggest moving the stuff on the bath tub or changing angle so it''s not in the photo. Love the creative here - it''s really nice work.  Cute model.', '2006-10-19 11:40:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943609, 411156, 6388, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. unfortunate that you can see the house in the background, but I guess the owner would have been upset if you bulldozed it for the photo and in basic editing you can''t get rid of it.<br/> <br/>love the way the light catches the first boat but seems to bypass the other.  very nice.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'Beautiful. unfortunate that you can see the house in the background, but I guess the owner would have been upset if you bulldozed it for the photo and in basic editing you can''t get rid of it. love the way the light catches the first boat but seems to bypass the other.  very nice. P', '2006-10-19 11:41:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943617, 411916, 6388, '<td valign="top">that''s some crazy-still water.  the muted tones are very nice.  I might have cropped it a little higher so the reflection was dominated by the land, but that''s just me.  I''m a little jealous that i wasn''t there.<br/> <br/>very nice.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'that''s some crazy-still water.  the muted tones are very nice.  I might have cropped it a little higher so the reflection was dominated by the land, but that''s just me.  I''m a little jealous that i wasn''t there. very nice. P', '2006-10-19 11:44:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943628, 410642, 31403, '<td valign="top">A kid waiting reluctantly for the bus in the morning is excellent creative - and a wonderful idea.  However the execution here is lacking.<br/> <br/>what story is your photo telling?  If it weren''t for the title I would have no idea there was a bus even involved here.  The photo alone is a overly lit girl walking with a backpack - I might assume school - <br/> <br/>The fact that I can''t see her face, there''s a reflective yellow sign distracting, and the underexposed background make it hard to give this a high score.<br/> <br/>To tell the story better you might include a bus stop sign, you could make one if you have to, or wait until the bus is there and shoot, or go to where the bus parks when it''s done with the daily rounds and stage a shoot there, have your model face the camera, use other light sources or wait until the lighting is more balanced to shoot.<br/> <br/>I understand that LITERALLY she IS waiting for the bus here - but that doesn''t necessarily make this a good photo - the more elements you can control the better your photo will tell the story.<br/> <br/>I hope that''s helpful.  If you already know all this sorry to be redundant.  I just like to explain and hopefully be helpful when I give low scores.  2</td>', 'A kid waiting reluctantly for the bus in the morning is excellent creative - and a wonderful idea.  However the execution here is lacking. what story is your photo telling?  If it weren''t for the title I would have no idea there was a bus even involved here.  The photo alone is a overly lit girl walking with a backpack - I might assume school -  The fact that I can''t see her face, there''s a reflective yellow sign distracting, and the underexposed background make it hard to give this a high score. To tell the story better you might include a bus stop sign, you could make one if you have to, or wait until the bus is there and shoot, or go to where the bus parks when it''s done with the daily rounds and stage a shoot there, have your model face the camera, use other light sources or wait until the lighting is more balanced to shoot. I understand that LITERALLY she IS waiting for the bus here - but that doesn''t necessarily make this a good photo - the more elements you can control the better your photo will tell the story. I hope that''s helpful.  If you already know all this sorry to be redundant.  I just like to explain and hopefully be helpful when I give low scores.  2', '2006-10-19 11:49:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943639, 411370, 31403, '<td valign="top">wow, that''s art!  I''ll bet it''s not being too well received by THIS crowd though.<br/> <br/>The background treatment is cool, cutting out the flesh tones and "plunking" them on top is disturbing to my eye.  I would like to see the photographic hand and arm blended a little more subtlely into the artistic background.<br/> <br/>If you hadn''t told me that was a slipper, I would have had no idea.  maybe slippers that were easier to "see" as slippers would help that - so go to the store and buy new stuff for every challenge would ya?  :-)<br/> <br/>I like the over all artistic approach, and I think the composition is cool. 6</td>', 'wow, that''s art!  I''ll bet it''s not being too well received by THIS crowd though. The background treatment is cool, cutting out the flesh tones and "plunking" them on top is disturbing to my eye.  I would like to see the photographic hand and arm blended a little more subtlely into the artistic background. If you hadn''t told me that was a slipper, I would have had no idea.  maybe slippers that were easier to "see" as slippers would help that - so go to the store and buy new stuff for every challenge would ya?  :-) I like the over all artistic approach, and I think the composition is cool. 6', '2006-10-19 11:53:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943653, 411149, 31403, '<td valign="top">this is tough to light - I think you''ve done a great job there.  Maybe softening those harsh highlights would have been helpful.<br/> <br/>My biggest suggestion is do something more with the crossaint (how do you spell that?).  I''d like to see the curve of the breakfast roll more closely match the curve of the plate - with no bite having been removed.  <br/> <br/>To me it would feel more commercial that way - but even with the bite removed I think you could place it more as a curve to accent the nice round lines in the rest of your composition.<br/> <br/>AH, that''s it - everything is nice and round except for the giant angle in the corner - there - give me three paragraphs and I''ll figure it out.  I''m leaving the whole ramble though so you can have a giant comment on your photo!  ;-P<br/> <br/>This is very nice work overall though - you should be proud to have this in your portfolio.  7</td>', 'this is tough to light - I think you''ve done a great job there.  Maybe softening those harsh highlights would have been helpful. My biggest suggestion is do something more with the crossaint (how do you spell that?).  I''d like to see the curve of the breakfast roll more closely match the curve of the plate - with no bite having been removed.   To me it would feel more commercial that way - but even with the bite removed I think you could place it more as a curve to accent the nice round lines in the rest of your composition. AH, that''s it - everything is nice and round except for the giant angle in the corner - there - give me three paragraphs and I''ll figure it out.  I''m leaving the whole ramble though so you can have a giant comment on your photo!  ;-P This is very nice work overall though - you should be proud to have this in your portfolio.  7', '2006-10-19 11:58:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943666, 412091, 31403, '<td valign="top">food photography is hard!  So you picked a tough one here!<br/> <br/>I think your yolk has some green in it that makes it quite the wrong color to be appetizing.  I would tweak that back to golden yellow and I think your photo here would be MUCH stronger.<br/> <br/>In general I would like to see more context to the subjet too.  Pull back so we can see the curve of the pan matching the curve of the egg, maybe the curve of the hot plate and chrome trim around the hot plate giving even more lines to your composition.  Then I think it would feel more a complete breakfast kind of shot too.  <br/> <br/>Overall I like the texture and composition here - hope that''s helpful</td>', 'food photography is hard!  So you picked a tough one here! I think your yolk has some green in it that makes it quite the wrong color to be appetizing.  I would tweak that back to golden yellow and I think your photo here would be MUCH stronger. In general I would like to see more context to the subjet too.  Pull back so we can see the curve of the pan matching the curve of the egg, maybe the curve of the hot plate and chrome trim around the hot plate giving even more lines to your composition.  Then I think it would feel more a complete breakfast kind of shot too.   Overall I like the texture and composition here - hope that''s helpful', '2006-10-19 12:02:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943671, 411908, 31403, '<td valign="top">nice creative - the darks have lost their detail, and the clock face feels like it has too.<br/> <br/>More detail in these areas would make this a much stronger photo, IMO.  Terrific idea - one I think we can all relate too!</td>', 'nice creative - the darks have lost their detail, and the clock face feels like it has too. More detail in these areas would make this a much stronger photo, IMO.  Terrific idea - one I think we can all relate too!', '2006-10-19 12:04:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943679, 411583, 31403, '<td valign="top">love the triangle of the trees on the left drawing my eye into the photo, and the further implied triangle of the pilings in the water.  <br/> <br/>The trees on the left are a little too dark, and tend to add weight to that side of the photo - but overall nice composition and beautiful colors.</td>', 'love the triangle of the trees on the left drawing my eye into the photo, and the further implied triangle of the pilings in the water.   The trees on the left are a little too dark, and tend to add weight to that side of the photo - but overall nice composition and beautiful colors.', '2006-10-19 12:06:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943687, 411772, 31403, '<td valign="top">I like the camera tilt, nice composition.<br/> <br/>Overall seems dingy - needs more white, like the background dodged all the way to white maybe - the saturation could be pushed too - I think the food would be more appetizing I think.<br/> <br/>Beans for breakfast?  One I haven''t tried before!  It does look good though!</td>', 'I like the camera tilt, nice composition. Overall seems dingy - needs more white, like the background dodged all the way to white maybe - the saturation could be pushed too - I think the food would be more appetizing I think. Beans for breakfast?  One I haven''t tried before!  It does look good though!', '2006-10-19 12:10:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943693, 410817, 31403, '<td valign="top">the black space at the top dilutes the impact of this image.  To me the light on the mane is the beauty here - and I would love the top of the image to cut the ears off, giving almost a square composition, but with very interesting lines and focusing my attention on what is cool.<br/> <br/>I''m a huge fan of horses, and love this shot otherwise.  I hope to own some of my own some day.  :-)  7</td>', 'the black space at the top dilutes the impact of this image.  To me the light on the mane is the beauty here - and I would love the top of the image to cut the ears off, giving almost a square composition, but with very interesting lines and focusing my attention on what is cool. I''m a huge fan of horses, and love this shot otherwise.  I hope to own some of my own some day.  :-)  7', '2006-10-19 12:12:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2943701, 411144, 31403, '<td valign="top">love the surprising reflection down amid the rocks - great compositional thought there.<br/> <br/>The shadows have gone through shadow/highlight?  It looks like they''ve been lighted too much, my eye expects to see darker shadows in this lighting - I''d leave a little more of the shadow in there.<br/> <br/>Very well done though overall.  7</td>', 'love the surprising reflection down amid the rocks - great compositional thought there. The shadows have gone through shadow/highlight?  It looks like they''ve been lighted too much, my eye expects to see darker shadows in this lighting - I''d leave a little more of the shadow in there. Very well done though overall.  7', '2006-10-19 12:14:52.000000', NULL, 1),
