(2964428, 412204, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>For the lighting setup you choose, the post processing of this image is perfect.  The shadows on the face and the lack of color gives this image a very mechanical feel and it fits well with the everyday, day in day out interaction you have with this machine.  The high lighting of your face draws my focus directly to your left eye, which has the effect of personalizing your daily routine for me.  There is nothing I can suggest for improving this image.  That in itself tells me that your score is directly linked to how the voters related to this image.  When you produce an image that conveys this much emotion and is so personal, you are bound to make some people a bit uncomfortable and they will vote accordingly.  Not being a member, I did vote on this challenge but I would have given it a 10, as few pictures at DPC convey the human side of photography like this.  Mine included.  Excuse me as I add this to my favorites.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, For the lighting setup you choose, the post processing of this image is perfect.  The shadows on the face and the lack of color gives this image a very mechanical feel and it fits well with the everyday, day in day out interaction you have with this machine.  The high lighting of your face draws my focus directly to your left eye, which has the effect of personalizing your daily routine for me.  There is nothing I can suggest for improving this image.  That in itself tells me that your score is directly linked to how the voters related to this image.  When you produce an image that conveys this much emotion and is so personal, you are bound to make some people a bit uncomfortable and they will vote accordingly.  Not being a member, I did vote on this challenge but I would have given it a 10, as few pictures at DPC convey the human side of photography like this.  Mine included.  Excuse me as I add this to my favorites. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-10-26 07:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2964430, 411671, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>As an optically challenged person, I can fully relate to your image and how morning first appears.  However, for those that arent optically challenged it is hard to relate your image to morning, as everything in the picture looks like it belongs in a spare room.  If this image had a more traditional bedroom setting or even a bathroom setting, it would have provided a stronger link to morning for those that don''t wear glasses.  On the technical side, I think your post processing work is exceptional and your idea was very creative.  You just didn''t connect your idea to the challenge topic strong enough for the whole population of voters at DPC.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, As an optically challenged person, I can fully relate to your image and how morning first appears.  However, for those that arent optically challenged it is hard to relate your image to morning, as everything in the picture looks like it belongs in a spare room.  If this image had a more traditional bedroom setting or even a bathroom setting, it would have provided a stronger link to morning for those that don''t wear glasses.  On the technical side, I think your post processing work is exceptional and your idea was very creative.  You just didn''t connect your idea to the challenge topic strong enough for the whole population of voters at DPC. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-10-26 07:55:08.000000', NULL, 0),
