(2967353, 411307, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>First, let me thank you for including so many details in your photographer''s comments.  Now for the critique.  My first impression is that this definitely looks like morning fog and has an interesting subject.  With nearly one third of your votes being a 5 and over half the votes in the 5 to 6 range, to me that indicates that the voters looked for literally 2-3 seconds and concluded, "this picture isn''t bad, so I can''t give 4 or less, but it doesn''t have a lot of wow, so I can''t give it a 7 or higher".  For some reason, black and white images didn''t score very well in this challenge.  I also see by the comments left during voting that the large amount of negative space above the trees was a love it or hate type thing.  It would have been safer to crop tighter on the trees, maybe in a landscape format, but the image might have lost some of its impact.  Personally I like the portrait format and wouldn''t change a thing.  You have a very good image that anyone at DPC would be proud to have in their portfolio.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, First, let me thank you for including so many details in your photographer''s comments.  Now for the critique.  My first impression is that this definitely looks like morning fog and has an interesting subject.  With nearly one third of your votes being a 5 and over half the votes in the 5 to 6 range, to me that indicates that the voters looked for literally 2-3 seconds and concluded, "this picture isn''t bad, so I can''t give 4 or less, but it doesn''t have a lot of wow, so I can''t give it a 7 or higher".  For some reason, black and white images didn''t score very well in this challenge.  I also see by the comments left during voting that the large amount of negative space above the trees was a love it or hate type thing.  It would have been safer to crop tighter on the trees, maybe in a landscape format, but the image might have lost some of its impact.  Personally I like the portrait format and wouldn''t change a thing.  You have a very good image that anyone at DPC would be proud to have in their portfolio. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-10-27 07:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2967967, 412204, 32754, '<td valign="top">This image was my favorite in the morning challenge...it was so personal and well photographed...the tones are just perfect and I congratulate you on an image that belonged in the top ten for its sheer reality and stunning compositional clarity...you could not have done better.</td>', 'This image was my favorite in the morning challenge...it was so personal and well photographed...the tones are just perfect and I congratulate you on an image that belonged in the top ten for its sheer reality and stunning compositional clarity...you could not have done better.', '2006-10-27 12:02:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2967981, 411910, 811, '<td valign="top">It''s well lit, and well focused, no so "complaints" there  The composition kinda doesn''t fit for me, though.  It feels out of balance.  The paper being upside down gives it a feeling of being an accident, and the cup being in the middle of the vertical frame both add to the unbalance, I think.  Maybe if the crop was a bit wider so that the whole cup was included (not that I mind things being out of frame)and if you had more of the window to the top and left.  Oh yea, turn the paper upside down.  Obviously just my opinion, because I''m not sure of the spatial constraints you had (or didn''t have).<br/> <br/>Did you realize you had almost a perfect voting bell curve on this picture?  I thought that was kind of interesting. <br/> <br/></td>', 'It''s well lit, and well focused, no so "complaints" there  The composition kinda doesn''t fit for me, though.  It feels out of balance.  The paper being upside down gives it a feeling of being an accident, and the cup being in the middle of the vertical frame both add to the unbalance, I think.  Maybe if the crop was a bit wider so that the whole cup was included (not that I mind things being out of frame)and if you had more of the window to the top and left.  Oh yea, turn the paper upside down.  Obviously just my opinion, because I''m not sure of the spatial constraints you had (or didn''t have). Did you realize you had almost a perfect voting bell curve on this picture?  I thought that was kind of interesting.  ', '2006-10-27 12:07:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2968001, 411772, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the tilt.  Of course, I''ve been accused of being "off-balance" anyway. :)  I think it adds "drama" and interest to the shot. :)<br/> <br/>The focus is good and the lighting is good.  I had no idea people ate baked beans for breakfast.  So the picture was educational as well.<br/> <br/>Wish I could offer something that would explain only a 5.5, but I''m not sure that I can.  Good work.</td>', 'I like the tilt.  Of course, I''ve been accused of being "off-balance" anyway. :)  I think it adds "drama" and interest to the shot. :) The focus is good and the lighting is good.  I had no idea people ate baked beans for breakfast.  So the picture was educational as well. Wish I could offer something that would explain only a 5.5, but I''m not sure that I can.  Good work.', '2006-10-27 12:15:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2968006, 412273, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the composition in this, and your use of negative space to the upper right.  The cup appears to be in focus, but for some reason my eyes are drawn to the handle, which is a bit soft, and that makes it look like the whole cup seem out of focus.<br/> <br/>The dog prints are cute!</td>', 'I like the composition in this, and your use of negative space to the upper right.  The cup appears to be in focus, but for some reason my eyes are drawn to the handle, which is a bit soft, and that makes it look like the whole cup seem out of focus. The dog prints are cute!', '2006-10-27 12:16:42.000000', NULL, 0),
