(2985972, 411567, 6999, '<td valign="top">Ah, those comments make me smile. I''m sure I remember commenting on this,  but whetever - I certainly remember looking at it. Some photos creep up on you, some slap you round the face and demand attention, and this one - well, it''s like when you suddenyl notice an old friend has been standing by your side for a while, and you don''t know where they arrived from.</td>', 'Ah, those comments make me smile. I''m sure I remember commenting on this,  but whetever - I certainly remember looking at it. Some photos creep up on you, some slap you round the face and demand attention, and this one - well, it''s like when you suddenyl notice an old friend has been standing by your side for a while, and you don''t know where they arrived from.', '2006-11-01 18:21:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2986320, 410470, 24111, '<td valign="top">I LOVE THIS!!! Hey , you make a great model and I completely understand about self portraits, we work without complaining and for free and yes, we are easily acessible! Ha!! Superb job!</td>', 'I LOVE THIS!!! Hey , you make a great model and I completely understand about self portraits, we work without complaining and for free and yes, we are easily acessible! Ha!! Superb job!', '2006-11-01 19:41:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2986566, 411732, 43869, '<td valign="top">I always love looking through your portfolio.  This is so amazing.   Not just the work that went into it, but the whole idea.  LOVE IT!</td>', 'I always love looking through your portfolio.  This is so amazing.   Not just the work that went into it, but the whole idea.  LOVE IT!', '2006-11-01 20:46:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989377, 411567, 30982, '<td valign="top">I quite like this one, but it takes more than one viewing to really appreciate it.  The DPC two-second view doesn''t cut it.  I seem to recall there were discussions that the sky was oversharpened - I disagree.<br/> <br/>First impression - when taken with the title, it''s somewhere I''d like to live if this is rush hour in the morning.  It appears lightly lived in yet deeply settled.  No mass rush, a few houses here and there amidst the trees, one tower in the distance.  The presentation leads one to think this one on/off ramp/curve is the only one serving this distant community, and that''s all it needs.<br/> <br/>The one commenter mentioned it''s hard to tell if it''s sea and sky or just sky - doesn''t matter.  If one wants to see it as sea and sky, it''s there.  Also doesn''t matter to me that it''s evening and not morning.  I can''t tell the difference without knowing the direction you''re facing and the B&amp;W disguises it even more.<br/> <br/>It''s quietly comfortable.  I think that pretty much goes with what Mr 301 said, too.</td>', 'I quite like this one, but it takes more than one viewing to really appreciate it.  The DPC two-second view doesn''t cut it.  I seem to recall there were discussions that the sky was oversharpened - I disagree. First impression - when taken with the title, it''s somewhere I''d like to live if this is rush hour in the morning.  It appears lightly lived in yet deeply settled.  No mass rush, a few houses here and there amidst the trees, one tower in the distance.  The presentation leads one to think this one on/off ramp/curve is the only one serving this distant community, and that''s all it needs. The one commenter mentioned it''s hard to tell if it''s sea and sky or just sky - doesn''t matter.  If one wants to see it as sea and sky, it''s there.  Also doesn''t matter to me that it''s evening and not morning.  I can''t tell the difference without knowing the direction you''re facing and the B&W disguises it even more. It''s quietly comfortable.  I think that pretty much goes with what Mr 301 said, too.', '2006-11-02 13:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989419, 411567, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i>The presentation leads one to think this one on/off ramp/curve is the only one serving this distant community, and that''s all it needs.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>so true! the best thing about this photo is the wonderful comments it is garnering...</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia:The presentation leads one to think this one on/off ramp/curve is the only one serving this distant community, and that''s all it needs.  so true! the best thing about this photo is the wonderful comments it is garnering...', '2006-11-02 13:59:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990201, 409522, 42567, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sabphoto:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bigdipper:</b></div><hr/><i> That looks too much like a sunset to work properly for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was taken just after the sun broke through the clouds in the morning.  I sure hope you did as the site recommends and voted it as it is a legal image and not what you thought it was.  <br/> <br/>Hate to think I lost points just because someone didn''t think it was morning. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think its a great picture!!  Looks very much like morning to me!  Awesome job</td>', 'Originally posted by sabphoto: Originally posted by bigdipper: That looks too much like a sunset to work properly for me.   This was taken just after the sun broke through the clouds in the morning.  I sure hope you did as the site recommends and voted it as it is a legal image and not what you thought it was.   Hate to think I lost points just because someone didn''t think it was morning.   I think its a great picture!!  Looks very much like morning to me!  Awesome job', '2006-11-02 17:30:39.000000', NULL, 0),
